---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy explaining how personal information is handled on this personal photography website."
  noindex={true}
>
  <section class="py-section" aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
    <div class="prose-container">
      <p class="meta-text mb-6">Legal</p>

      <h1 id="privacy-heading" class="font-display text-display-xl text-text-primary mb-8">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>



      <div class="space-y-8 text-body-md text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-display-md text-text-primary mb-4">Overview</h2>
          <p>
            This is a personal photography website. It does not sell products, process payments, or require user accounts. This policy explains how any personal information you provide is handled.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-display-md text-text-primary mb-4">Information Collection</h2>
          <p>
            The only personal information collected is what you voluntarily provide through the contact form: your name, email address, and message content. This information is used solely to reply to you.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-display-md text-text-primary mb-4">Cookies & Analytics</h2>
          <p>
            This site uses Microsoft Clarity and Google Analytics to understand how visitors use the site. Essential cookies may also be used by the hosting provider (Cloudflare) for security purposes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-display-md text-text-primary mb-4">What your browser remembers</h2>
          <p>
            A few small things are kept in your own browser's storage so the site behaves the same next
            time: your light or dark theme, and which photograph the home page showed last. If you switch
            on <a href="/labs">Labs</a>, it also remembers that choice, which photographs you have opened,
            which ones existed at your last visit (so it can mark new ones), and your results in the
            games. None of this is sent anywhere. Clearing your
            browser's site data removes it, and the Labs page has a button that forgets what you have seen.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            Two Labs experiments go a little further, and still keep everything on your device. Colour
            match uses your camera only after you press its button and your browser asks you; each
            picture is read on your phone or computer to find its colours, and is never recorded,
            stored or sent. What you write on a postcard goes into the picture you make and nowhere
            else.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-display-md text-text-primary mb-4">Third Parties</h2>
          <p>
            No personal data is shared with, sold to, or disclosed to third parties. The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, which may process standard HTTP request metadata (IP addresses, user agents) in accordance with their own privacy policy.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-display text-display-md text-text-primary mb-4">Contact</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions about this privacy policy, please <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="text-caption text-text-secondary/60 pt-4 border-t border-subtle">
          Last updated: September 2026. This policy was written by me (Vasu Ambasana).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
